A, Miller RD, Cohen NH (Hrsg) (2020) Miller’s anesthesia. Elsevier, Philadelphia, PA [ Google Scholar ] 28. West JB (2012) Respiratory physiology: the essentials, 9. Aufl. Wolters Kluwer Health/Lippincott Williams & Wilkins, Philadelphia [ Google Scholar ] 29. Riva T, Pedersen TH, Seiler S, Kasper N, Theiler L, Greif R et al (2018) Transnasal humidified rapid insufflation ventilatory exchange for oxygenation of children during apnoea: a prospective randomised controlled trial. Br J Anaesth 120:592–599 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Uzun DD, Hezel F, Weigand MA, Schmitt FCF (2024) Apnoische Oxygenierung – Sicherheit durch Standard! Notfall Rettungsmed. 10.1007/s10049-024-01385-4 [ Google Scholar ] 31. Çekmen N (2023) Apneic oxygenation and anesthesia: mini review. https://www.jscimedcentral.com/public/assets/articles/anesthesiology-11-1122.pdf 32. Disma N, Asai T, Cools E, Cronin A, Engelhardt T, Fiadjoe J et al (2024) Airway management in neonates and infants: European society of anaesthesiology and intensive care and British journal of anaesthesia joint guidelines. Eur J Anaesthesiol 41:3–23 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials 101_2025_1529_MOESM1_ESM.pdf (2.6MB, pdf) Fragenkatalog zum Online Survey Apnoische Oxygenierung, Version 1.0, Stand 01.06.2024 Data Availability Statement Die im Rahmen der Studie erfassten Daten können in begründeten Fällen vom korrespondierenden Autor erhalten werden.',6,'2025-10-15 11:52:10','2025-10-15 11:52:10');
