. 11, 65-66. 10.1080/15265161.2011.578468 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Pratt, B. and Hyder, A. A. (2015). Reinterpreting responsiveness for health systems research in low and middle-income countries. Bioethics, 29, 379-388. 10.1111/bioe.12138 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Reynolds, J. M. and Wieseler, C. (2022). The Disability Bioethics Reader . Routledge & CRC Press. [ Google Scholar ] Sharp, R. R., Scott, A. L., Landy, D. C. and Kicklighter, L. A. (2008). Who is buying bioethics research? Am. J. Bioeth. 8, 54-58; discussion W1-2. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Shea, L.-M. (2020). No perfect syllabus for distance learning: DBT skills for deciding how to teach throughout uncertainty. Pedagogy and the Human Sciences 7, 1-12. [ Google Scholar ] Tarazi, S., Aguilera-Castrejon, A., Joubran, C., Ghanem, N., Ashouokhi, S., Roncato, F., Wildschutz, E., Haddad, M., Oldak, B., Gomez-Cesar, E.et al. (2022). Post-gastrulation synthetic embryos generated ex utero from mouse naive ESCs. Cell, 185, 3290-3306.e25. 10.1016/j.cell.2022.07.028 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Tolchin, B., Latham, S. R., Bruce, L., Ferrante, L. E., Kraschel, K., Jubanyik, K., Hull, S. C., Herbst, J. L., Kapo, J., Moritz, E. D.et al. (2020). Developing a triage protocol for the COVID-19 pandemic: allocating scarce medical resources in a public health emergency. J. Clin. Ethics 31, 303-317. 10.1086/JCE2020314303 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Uba, K. and Bosi, L. (2022). Explaining youth radicalism as a positioning of the self at opposite extremes. Politics, 42, 128-145. 10.1177/0263395721990539 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] Vrselja, Z., Daniele, S. G., Silbereis, J., Talpo, F., Morozov, Y. M., Sousa, A. M. M., Tanaka, B. S., Skarica, M., Pletikos, M., Kaur, N.et al. (2019). Restoration of brain circulation and cellular functions hours post-mortem. Nature 568, 336-343. 10.1038/s41586-019-1099-1 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar