onsibility.pdf?sfvrsn=6 ; Accessed 13 April 2022. 56. Catholic Health Association and Practice Greenhealt. Environmental Sustainability: Getting Started Guide. St. Louis: The Catholic Health Association of the United States; 2010. 57. Catholic Health Association of the United States . Faithfully Healing the Earth: Catholic Health Care and Climate Change. Washington, DC: Catholic Health Association; 2009. [ Google Scholar ] 58. Catholic Health Initiatives. Environmental Stewardship. 2014. http://catholichealthinit.org/environmental-stewardship , Accessed 13 April 2022. 59. NHS Sustainable Development Unit. Saving Carbon, Improving Health: NHS Carbon Reduction Strategy for England. London: NHS Sustainable Development Unit; 2019. 60. Anderko L, Chalupka S, Afzal BM. Climate Change and Health: Is there a Role for the Health Care Sector? St. Louis: Catholic Health Association of the United States; 2012. 61. Jahr, Fritz. Bio-Ethics—Reviewing the Ethical Relations of Humans Towards Animals and Plants. JAHR-European Journal of Bioethics. 2010;1(2):227–231. (originally published as Jahr F. Bio-Ethik. Eine Umschau uber die ethischen Beziehungen des Menschen zu Tier und Pflanze. Kosmos. Handweise fur Naturfreunde und Zentralblatt fur das naturwissenschaftliche Bildungs- und Sammelwesen Kosmos: Gesellschaft der Naturfreunde. Stuttgart volume. 1927;24: 2–4.) 62. Potter VR. Bioethics: Bridge to the Future. New Jersey: Prentice-Hall; 1971. [ Google Scholar ] 63. Callahan D. Sustainable Medicine. Project Syndicate. 2004. https://www.project-syndicate.org/commentary/sustainable-medicine?barrier=accesspaylog . Accessed 13 April 2022. 64. Richie C. Principles of Green Bioethics: Sustainability in Health Care. East Lansing: Michigan State University Press; 2019. [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Data Availability Statement Not applicable.',3,'2025-10-20 05:50:10